  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Key operating and financial data' summary table (audited), cross-validated against the Balance Sheet wherever available. This bank has operated with deeply negative shareholders' equity and a deeply negative Capital Adequacy Ratio (CAR) throughout the entire researched period (2013-2024), i.e. it has been technically insolvent by conventional accounting/regulatory measures for over a decade — a legacy of the 2006 collapse and nationalization of its predecessor, The Oriental Bank Limited, on fraud/mismanagement grounds. As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investments' rather than 'NPL'. The only year in the researched series with a positive operating profit (before provisions), though still a net loss after tax and provisions. The 2024 annual report's own 'Key operating and financial data of at least preceding 5 years' table has a demonstrated one-year column-shift error for its FY2022/FY2021/FY2020 columns (each showing the prior year's real figures under the wrong year label, confirmed by cross-checking against each of those years' own annual report and against the FY2023/FY2022/FY2021 reports' own first-column data, which are mutually consistent and used here instead). The FY2024 and FY2023 columns of that table are correctly aligned.",
